---
import StandardLifecycleNotice from "../../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import StandardPageLayout from "../../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../../data/standards/hgb/drs09.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  subtitle={metadata.nativeTitle}
  framework="hgb"
  status={metadata.status}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Part of the DRS consolidation wave" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Why withdrawn" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Status summary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <StandardLifecycleNotice
    type="withdrawn"
    explanation="This standard has been withdrawn."
    
    
    
  />

  <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Part of the DRS consolidation wave</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card warn">
<div class="ctitle">Part of the DRS consolidation wave</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 9, first announced 11 December 2001, elaborated the proportionate consolidation mechanics for jointly-managed enterprises established under §310 HGB, covered in detail in the earlier HGB poster series – the genuine election (unlike full consolidation's mandatory 100% approach) allowing a joint venturer to bring in only its own percentage share of each underlying asset and liability line by line.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Why withdrawn – a clean, confirmed handoff</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card info">
<div class="ctitle">Why withdrawn – a clean, confirmed handoff</div>
<div class="principle">This is one of the most cleanly documented replacements in this consolidation wave: DRS 9 was formally withdrawn upon the BMJV's 17 July 2018 Bundesanzeiger announcement of DRS 27 "Anteilmäßige Konsolidierung," with DRS 9 remaining applicable for the LAST time only to fiscal years beginning on or before 31 December 2019 – a genuine, confirmed one-to-one handoff between predecessor and successor, unlike some of the earlier, more consolidative replacements in this wave.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Status summary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card">
<div class="ctitle">Status summary</div>
<div class="td-table">
<div class="th"><span>Field</span><span>Detail</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Original topic</span><span>Proportionate consolidation for jointly-managed enterprises</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>First announced</span><span>11 December 2001</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Last amended (as DRS 9)</span><span>DRÄS 8, 2017</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Withdrawn / successor</span><span><strong>DRS 27 – Anteilmäßige Konsolidierung</strong> (17.07.2018)</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Last applicable</span><span>Fiscal years beginning on or before 31.12.2019</span></div>
</div>
</div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
